{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-32591","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45720","text":"TRAAVIIS — Environment Authoring Closure ("},{"id":"spn-45721","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs init"},{"id":"spn-45722","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-45723","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-45724","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-32592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45725","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date"},{"id":"spn-45726","text":" 2026-07-24 · "},{"id":"spn-45727","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status"},{"id":"spn-45728","text":" shipped, 34 new laws green, full suite green "},{"id":"spn-45729","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope"},{"id":"spn-45730","text":" RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md §5, §5a, §6 — the first two items of the deferred surface that §7's build order unblocks once "},{"id":"spn-45731","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-45732","text":" exists."}]},{"id":"blk-32593","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45733","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"id":"blk-32594","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45734","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-45735","text":" closed the beachhead: one agent, one frozen subject, one content-addressed receipt. But every bundle it could run had to be "},{"id":"spn-45736","marks":["italic"],"text":"hand-built"},{"id":"spn-45737","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-45738","marks":["code"],"text":"examples/eval-one/residency-forge/build_bundle.py"},{"id":"spn-45739","text":"). Authoring was the gap."}]},{"id":"blk-32595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45740","text":"Two commands close it, and the split between them is the whole design:"}]},{"id":"blk-32596","kind":"code","language":"sh","text":"trvs init --list                                  # templates + their substrates\ntrvs init --template evidence-residency my-env    # seeds a subject + skeletons\ntrvs pack my-env my-env-pkg                       # closes it into a package\ntrvs eval-one my-env-pkg --agent … --platform linux-x86_64"},{"id":"blk-32597","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45741","text":"Verified end to end, from nothing to a scored episode:"}]},{"id":"blk-32598","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"init  →  8 files, identity: unresolved (init derives none)\npack  →  env-a38ec4c0…  snapshot snap-c66198ab…  task task-3b4b2599…\n         closure  ✓ verified before write\n         reopened ✓ re-derived from the written bytes\neval-one → status ✓ ok · validity valid · reward 1\n           citations pass · patch pass · tests pass · identity pass ·\n           finding_completeness pass"},{"id":"blk-32599","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45742","text":"The scaffolded residency subject recomputes to "},{"id":"spn-45743","marks":["bold"],"text":"exactly"},{"id":"spn-45744","text":" the frozen example's "},{"id":"spn-45745","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-c66198abf3ef6153d4bd6033fa40a0bd0028df3a7699ab645dc947710e51cba4"},{"id":"spn-45746","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-45747","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-25c4ce1276a7b70a473548354ae5d14f1c852ba087ffd09bc9b17b550c5c05a5"},{"id":"spn-45748","text":", and the "},{"id":"spn-45749","marks":["code"],"text":"golden-spinner"},{"id":"spn-45750","text":" template lowers to the frozen demo world "},{"id":"spn-45751","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9cbc5fd086ce4356d…fe4a"},{"id":"spn-45752","text":". The seeds are the real artifacts, not lookalikes."}]},{"id":"blk-32600","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45753","text":"2. The load-bearing decision: "},{"id":"spn-45754","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-45755","text":" derives nothing"}]},{"id":"blk-32601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45756","text":"§6 says "},{"id":"spn-45757","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-45758","text":" \"invents no identity.\" Taken literally that forbids the obvious implementation — scaffolding a "},{"id":"spn-45759","marks":["code"],"text":"task.json"},{"id":"spn-45760","text":" with a "},{"id":"spn-45761","marks":["code"],"text":"reward_id"},{"id":"spn-45762","text":" in it — because a scaffold cannot know the hash of bytes the author has not written yet, and a placeholder hash is a lie that later verifies."}]},{"id":"blk-32602","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45763","text":"So the scaffold emits "},{"id":"spn-45764","marks":["bold"],"text":"references"},{"id":"spn-45765","text":", and packing is the substitution:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-32604","spans":[{"id":"spn-45766","text":"scaffold ("},{"id":"spn-45767","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-45768","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-32605","spans":[{"id":"spn-45769","text":"package ("},{"id":"spn-45770","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-45771","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-32603","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-32606","spans":[{"id":"spn-45772","marks":["code"],"text":"task.reward_spec: \"reward.json\""}]},{"id":"blk-32607","spans":[{"id":"spn-45773","marks":["code"],"text":"task.reward_id: \"rew-…\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-32608","spans":[{"id":"spn-45774","marks":["code"],"text":"subject.snapshot_def: \"snapshot_def.json\""}]},{"id":"blk-32609","spans":[{"id":"spn-45775","marks":["code"],"text":"subject.snapshot_id: \"snap-…\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-32610","spans":[{"id":"spn-45776","marks":["code"],"text":"identity_policy…"},{"id":"spn-45777","text":" "},{"id":"spn-45778","marks":["italic"],"text":"(no `before_id`)"}]},{"id":"blk-32611","spans":[{"id":"spn-45779","marks":["code"],"text":"before_id: \"sem-…\""},{"id":"spn-45780","text":" (lowered now)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32612","spans":[{"id":"spn-45781","marks":["italic"],"text":"(no `env_id`)"}]},{"id":"blk-32613","spans":[{"id":"spn-45782","marks":["code"],"text":"env_id: \"env-…\""}]}]]},{"id":"blk-32614","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45783","text":"That is why "},{"id":"spn-45784","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-45785","text":" needs no engine and "},{"id":"spn-45786","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-45787","text":" does. It also makes L1 mechanically checkable: "},{"id":"spn-45788","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.identity_violations()"},{"id":"spn-45789","text":" scans every emitted document for an identity "},{"id":"spn-45790","marks":["italic"],"text":"key"},{"id":"spn-45791","text":" at any depth "},{"id":"spn-45792","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-45793","text":" every emitted byte for an id-shaped literal, so a future template cannot quietly bake one in — including in prose."}]},{"id":"blk-32615","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45794","text":"The literal half fails "},{"id":"spn-45795","marks":["bold"],"text":"closed"},{"id":"spn-45796","text":". It used to be a "},{"id":"spn-45797","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-[0-9a-f]{8,}"},{"id":"spn-45798","text":" regex, which matches a well-formed digest and "},{"id":"spn-45799","marks":["italic"],"text":"nothing else"},{"id":"spn-45800","text":": a rung-prefixed token it could not parse — "},{"id":"spn-45801","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-abcdef12ZZZ"},{"id":"spn-45802","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45803","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-ABCDEF1234567890"},{"id":"spn-45804","text":", or the same id under a changed grammar ("},{"id":"spn-45805","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-jcs1-…"},{"id":"spn-45806","text":") — produced no match, and a guard that finds no id reports no violation, so a typo and a scheme change both read as \"clean\". "},{"id":"spn-45807","marks":["code"],"text":"scaffold.id_tokens"},{"id":"spn-45808","text":" now recognises the "},{"id":"spn-45809","marks":["bold"],"text":"rung prefix first"},{"id":"spn-45810","text":" (from the one "},{"id":"spn-45811","marks":["code"],"text":"ID_RUNGS"},{"id":"spn-45812","text":" list, which "},{"id":"spn-45813","marks":["code"],"text":"test_scaffold"},{"id":"spn-45814","text":"'s L1c pins against the ids "},{"id":"spn-45815","marks":["code"],"text":"identity.py"},{"id":"spn-45816","text":" actually mints) and then asks whether the remainder is a digest. Three verdicts: "},{"id":"spn-45817","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-45818","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45819","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-45820","text":" (a known rung whose remainder does not parse) and "},{"id":"spn-45821","marks":["code"],"text":"unknown"},{"id":"spn-45822","text":" (a digest under a rung nobody should have minted). All three are violations. The elision form "},{"id":"spn-45823","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-45824","text":" is deliberately "},{"id":"spn-45825","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-45826","text":" a token — writing \"an id goes here\" asserts none."}]},{"id":"blk-32616","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45827","text":"What the guard does not report, and why that is written down"}]},{"id":"blk-32617","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45828","text":"The first version of this rewrite claimed the three verdicts \"leave no token that is both id-shaped and unreported\". That sentence was false in "},{"id":"spn-45829","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-45830","text":" directions, and each direction is a way a guard stops guarding:"}]},{"id":"blk-32618","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45831","text":"It was "},{"id":"spn-45832","marks":["bold"],"text":"narrower than the regex it replaced"},{"id":"spn-45833","text":". A lookbehind refused to begin"}]}],"id":"blk-32619","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32621","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45834","text":"a token after "},{"id":"spn-45835","marks":["code"],"text":"-"},{"id":"spn-45836","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-45837","marks":["code"],"text":"."},{"id":"spn-45838","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-45839","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-42d0bb07e5f83e9e"},{"id":"spn-45840","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-45841","marks":["code"],"text":"run.episode-42d0bb07e5f83e9e"},{"id":"spn-45842","text":" — which the old "},{"id":"spn-45843","marks":["code"],"text":"\\b"},{"id":"spn-45844","text":"-anchored regex reported — came back as "},{"id":"spn-45845","marks":["code"],"text":"[]"},{"id":"spn-45846","text":". A real, well-formed id, completely unreported. The lookbehind was standing in for something genuine ("},{"id":"spn-45847","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.finding- completeness-impl.v1"},{"id":"spn-45848","text":" is a declared verifier version present in every "},{"id":"spn-45849","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-45850","text":", and reading it as the "},{"id":"spn-45851","marks":["code"],"text":"finding"},{"id":"spn-45852","text":" rung failed "},{"id":"spn-45853","marks":["code"],"text":"test_compare"},{"id":"spn-45854","text":"'s C20), but it paid for that with coverage and no law recorded the trade."}]},{"id":"blk-32622","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32624","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45855","text":"It was "},{"id":"spn-45856","marks":["bold"],"text":"wider on prose"},{"id":"spn-45857","text":". Every hyphenated phrase whose first word happened"}]}],"id":"blk-32623","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32625","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45858","text":"to be a rung name — "},{"id":"spn-45859","marks":["code"],"text":"env-vars"},{"id":"spn-45860","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45861","marks":["code"],"text":"task-oriented"},{"id":"spn-45862","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45863","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-apply"},{"id":"spn-45864","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45865","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-ver"},{"id":"spn-45866","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45867","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-path"},{"id":"spn-45868","text":" — was reported as a malformed id. A guard that cries wolf is switched off by the next person to trip it, which is fail-open by a slower route. Swept over this repository plus its build artifacts and sealed bundles (~56,000 documents), the rewrite produced "},{"id":"spn-45869","marks":["bold"],"text":"419"},{"id":"spn-45870","text":" non-"},{"id":"spn-45871","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-45872","text":" verdicts where the current guard produces "},{"id":"spn-45873","marks":["bold"],"text":"29"},{"id":"spn-45874","text":". The ~60 distinct tokens it dropped are all prose or identifiers — "},{"id":"spn-45875","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-bundle"},{"id":"spn-45876","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45877","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-fixture"},{"id":"spn-45878","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45879","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-ver"},{"id":"spn-45880","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45881","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-fail"},{"id":"spn-45882","text":" — including "},{"id":"spn-45883","marks":["bold"],"text":"`task-b`, which appears in real packed `env.json` and `TRAAVIIS_BUNDLE.json` documents"},{"id":"spn-45884","text":": the rewrite called a task "},{"id":"spn-45885","marks":["italic"],"text":"filename"},{"id":"spn-45886","text":" a malformed id. What survives as "},{"id":"spn-45887","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-45888","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-45889","marks":["code"],"text":"*-PLACEHOLDER"},{"id":"spn-45890","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45891","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-abcdef12ZZZ"},{"id":"spn-45892","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45893","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-ABCDEF1234567890"},{"id":"spn-45894","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-45895","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-jcs1-…"},{"id":"spn-45896","text":" — every one an id-shaped token, and none of them prose."}]},{"id":"blk-32626","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45897","text":"The first defect is not visible as a count, and saying so is part of the record: committed text almost never writes an id inside a compound, which is exactly why nobody noticed it was no longer being read. It is demonstrated instead by planting — "},{"id":"spn-45898","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-<64 hex>"},{"id":"spn-45899","text":" written into a real scaffolded template and into a real "},{"id":"spn-45900","marks":["code"],"text":"ComparisonV1"},{"id":"spn-45901","text":", where the legacy regex reports it, the rewrite reports nothing, and the current guard reports it again."}]},{"id":"blk-32627","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45902","text":"The discrimination that keeps both properties is the "},{"id":"spn-45903","marks":["bold"],"text":"remainder's shape"},{"id":"spn-45904","text":", with position gating only the "},{"id":"spn-45905","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"},{"id":"spn-45906","text":" verdict and never the "},{"id":"spn-45907","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-45908","text":" one:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-32629","spans":[{"id":"spn-45909","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-32630","spans":[{"id":"spn-45910","text":"reported"}]}],"id":"blk-32628","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-32631","spans":[{"id":"spn-45911","text":"a well-formed digest, anywhere — "},{"id":"spn-45912","marks":["code"],"text":"prev-episode-<hex>"},{"id":"spn-45913","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45914","marks":["code"],"text":"run.episode-<hex>"}]},{"id":"blk-32632","spans":[{"id":"spn-45915","marks":["bold"],"text":"yes"},{"id":"spn-45916","text":", as "},{"id":"spn-45917","marks":["code"],"text":"id"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32633","spans":[{"id":"spn-45918","text":"a rung + a remainder bearing a digit, an uppercase letter, or a run ≥ 16"}]},{"id":"blk-32634","spans":[{"id":"spn-45919","marks":["bold"],"text":"yes"},{"id":"spn-45920","text":", as "},{"id":"spn-45921","marks":["code"],"text":"malformed"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32635","spans":[{"id":"spn-45922","text":"a rung + lowercase words of ordinary length — "},{"id":"spn-45923","marks":["code"],"text":"env-vars"},{"id":"spn-45924","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45925","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-nonsense"}]},{"id":"blk-32636","spans":[{"id":"spn-45926","text":"no"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32637","spans":[{"id":"spn-45927","text":"a rung "},{"id":"spn-45928","marks":["italic"],"text":"embedded"},{"id":"spn-45929","text":" in a compound name without a digest — "},{"id":"spn-45930","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.finding-completeness-impl.v1"},{"id":"spn-45931","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45932","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis-snap-01uu24ob"}]},{"id":"blk-32638","spans":[{"id":"spn-45933","text":"no"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-32639","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45934","text":"The third row is a "},{"id":"spn-45935","marks":["bold"],"text":"stated trade, not a discrimination"},{"id":"spn-45936","text":": "},{"id":"spn-45937","marks":["code"],"text":"nonsense"},{"id":"spn-45938","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-45939","marks":["code"],"text":"oriented"},{"id":"spn-45940","text":" are both eight lowercase letters with the same hex-letter density, and no lexical rule separates a typo'd id whose remainder happens to be word-shaped from an English phrase. What bounds the silence is that one edit in any direction — a digit, an uppercase letter, a longer run, an actual digest — puts the token back in scope. A mangled sha256 keeps its digits; a word has none. Both silences are pinned by "},{"id":"spn-45941","marks":["code"],"text":"test_scaffold"},{"id":"spn-45942","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-45943","marks":["bold"],"text":"L1g"},{"id":"spn-45944","text":", and the boundary by "},{"id":"spn-45945","marks":["bold"],"text":"L1e"},{"id":"spn-45946","text":", so widening either has to move a law rather than a comment."}]},{"id":"blk-32640","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45947","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-45948","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-45949","text":" follows §6's order literally"}]},{"id":"blk-32641","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"1. validate_subject             well-formed for the profile\n2. recompute_subject_identity   snap-… / sem-… FROM THE BYTES\n3. bind + close                 rew-… → task-… → env-…\n4. verify_closure               every reference resolves\n--- nothing has been written yet ---\n5. write                        temp tree → one os.replace\n6. reopen_package               re-derive every id from what landed on disk"},{"id":"blk-32642","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45950","text":"Step 6 is not ceremony. "},{"id":"spn-45951","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-45952","text":" deliberately does not trust its own in-memory computation: it reads the package back, re-derives "},{"id":"spn-45953","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-45954","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-45955","marks":["code"],"text":"task-"},{"id":"spn-45956","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-45957","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-"},{"id":"spn-45958","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-45959","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-"},{"id":"spn-45960","text":" from the written bytes, "},{"id":"spn-45961","marks":["bold"],"text":"rebuilds the snapshot from the written subject tree"},{"id":"spn-45962","text":", and re-lowers the written world. If any of that disagrees, the package is removed and the command fails. Tampering with a packed task, or with one byte of a packed subject, is caught ("},{"id":"spn-45963","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_TASK_ID"},{"id":"spn-45964","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45965","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_SUBJECT_BYTES"},{"id":"spn-45966","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-32643","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45967","text":"Everything is fail-closed with a typed code: "},{"id":"spn-45968","marks":["code"],"text":"SOURCE_PREBOUND"},{"id":"spn-45969","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45970","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_DRIFT"},{"id":"spn-45971","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45972","marks":["code"],"text":"SUBJECT_KIND"},{"id":"spn-45973","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45974","marks":["code"],"text":"CLOSURE_VERIFIER"},{"id":"spn-45975","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45976","marks":["code"],"text":"CLOSURE_SUBJECT_BINDING"},{"id":"spn-45977","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45978","marks":["code"],"text":"SPLIT_UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"spn-45979","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45980","marks":["code"],"text":"DEST_NOT_EMPTY"},{"id":"spn-45981","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45982","marks":["code"],"text":"ENGINE_UNAVAILABLE"},{"id":"spn-45983","text":", "},{"id":"spn-45984","marks":["code"],"text":"REOPEN_*"},{"id":"spn-45985","text":". A refused pack writes nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-32644","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-45986","text":"4. The §5a admission interface is real"}]},{"id":"blk-32645","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45987","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"},{"id":"spn-45988","text":" implements "},{"id":"spn-45989","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_subject · verify_closure · recompute_subject_identity · reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-45990","text":" as a base class plus two profiles:"}]},{"id":"blk-32646","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32648","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45991","marks":["code"],"text":"trvm.world.v1"},{"id":"spn-45992","text":" — subject is WRL source; identity is "},{"id":"spn-45993","marks":["code"],"text":"engine.lower_source()"},{"id":"spn-45994","text":" →"}]}],"id":"blk-32647","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32649","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45995","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-45996","text":"; reopen re-lowers the written world."}]},{"id":"blk-32650","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32652","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45997","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-45998","text":" — subject is a repository; identity is"}]}],"id":"blk-32651","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32653","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-45999","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot.build_snapshot()"},{"id":"spn-46000","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-46001","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-46002","text":"; reopen rebuilds it from the written tree; closure additionally checks the verifier plan is "},{"id":"spn-46003","marks":["italic"],"text":"answerable by the reward it is bound to"},{"id":"spn-46004","text":" and that the test plan declares a runner profile."}]},{"id":"blk-32654","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46005","text":"The packer branches on profile in exactly two places (which subject bytes to copy, and the eval-bundle emission). A third substrate is a new profile object, not a new branch — which was the point of §5a."}]},{"id":"blk-32655","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46006","text":"5. Laws (34 new, all green)"}]},{"id":"blk-32656","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46007","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_scaffold.py"},{"id":"spn-46008","text":" — 16 laws: L1 invents no identity (incl. a planted-id detector test, so the check itself is proven to fire) · L2 deterministic (pure + on-disk) · L3 substrate-distinct · L4 declared frozen versions · L5 fail-closed + atomic (non-empty dest refused, mid-write failure leaves no partial tree and no temp dir) · L6 admissible input (snapshot definition matches the seeded tree exactly; both seeded worlds lower) · L7 portable (no absolute/host paths) · plus the CLI contract."}]},{"id":"blk-32657","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46009","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_pack.py"},{"id":"spn-46010","text":" — 18 laws: P1 every id recomputed, pre-bound ids refused · P2 content moves identity (subject bytes → "},{"id":"spn-46011","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-"},{"id":"spn-46012","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-46013","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-46014","text":"; task instructions → "},{"id":"spn-46015","marks":["code"],"text":"task-"},{"id":"spn-46016","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-46017","marks":["code"],"text":"env-"},{"id":"spn-46018","text":") · "},{"id":"spn-46019","marks":["bold"],"text":"P3 presentation does NOT move `env-`"},{"id":"spn-46020","text":" (renaming + rewriting the description is byte-for-byte the same "},{"id":"spn-46021","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-46022","text":") · P4/P5 closure verified before write, nothing written on refusal, subject drift caught · P6 tampering fails reopen (task and subject) · P7 "},{"id":"spn-46023","marks":["code"],"text":"before_id"},{"id":"spn-46024","text":" is computed, and a declared one is refused · P8 determinism · P9 the TRVM profile lowers + reopens, and is a typed failure with no engine · P10 the packed environment actually runs to reward 1.0."}]},{"id":"blk-32658","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46025","text":"Regression: full suite green — identity 25, snapshot 10, reward 17, admission 16, paths 10, execfacts 8, vcontext 5, patchapply 10, verifiers 15, runner 10, evalone 14, substrate_verifiers 24, forge_adapter 6, cli_evalone 18, real_residency 9, episode_evidence 56."}]},{"id":"blk-32659","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46026","text":"6. Autonomous decisions — flagged for GPT-5.6"}]},{"id":"blk-32660","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32662","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46027","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scaffold-level references + `residency.snapshot-def.v1`."},{"id":"spn-46028","text":" §5 names a"}]}],"id":"blk-32661","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-32663","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46029","text":"\"snapshot definition\" as the scaffolded residency artifact; I gave it its own version string rather than emitting a "},{"id":"spn-46030","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.snapshot.v1"},{"id":"spn-46031","text":" with empty hashes. Confirm the name."}]},{"id":"blk-32664","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32666","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46032","marks":["bold"],"text":"`env-` identity allowlist excludes `name` and `description`."},{"id":"spn-46033","text":" §5 says"}]}],"id":"blk-32665","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-32667","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46034","text":"presentation-only edits move "},{"id":"spn-46035","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-46036","text":" only, so this is implemented as an explicit allowlist (like "},{"id":"spn-46037","marks":["code"],"text":"canonicalize_episode"},{"id":"spn-46038","text":") rather than by convention. Confirm "},{"id":"spn-46039","marks":["code"],"text":"name"},{"id":"spn-46040","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-46041","marks":["code"],"text":"description"},{"id":"spn-46042","text":" are presentation."}]},{"id":"blk-32668","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32670","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46043","marks":["bold"],"text":"`bundle-…` is not implemented."},{"id":"spn-46044","text":" "},{"id":"spn-46045","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-46046","text":" emits a package "},{"id":"spn-46047","marks":["italic"],"text":"directory"},{"id":"spn-46048","text":" and an"}]}],"id":"blk-32669","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-32671","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46049","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-46050","text":"; the outer content-addressed distributed package id from D3 is still open. This is the remaining half of §5 and I did not invent it."}]},{"id":"blk-32672","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32674","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46051","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single-task residency packages also emit `bundle.json`"},{"id":"spn-46052","text":" so "},{"id":"spn-46053","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-46054","text":" output is"}]}],"id":"blk-32673","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-32675","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46055","text":"directly runnable by "},{"id":"spn-46056","marks":["code"],"text":"eval-one"},{"id":"spn-46057","text":". Multi-task packages do "},{"id":"spn-46058","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-46059","text":" get one (they would need a split-runner, i.e. "},{"id":"spn-46060","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-46061","text":") — deferred rather than emitted half-true."}]},{"id":"blk-32676","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32678","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46062","marks":["bold"],"text":"`pack` soft-loads the engine."},{"id":"spn-46063","text":" "},{"id":"spn-46064","marks":["code"],"text":"ENGINE_UNAVAILABLE"},{"id":"spn-46065","text":" is a typed admission"}]}],"id":"blk-32677","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-32679","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46066","text":"failure, so a residency pack that needs no lowering still works on a machine with no TRVM checkout."}]},{"id":"blk-32680","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32682","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46067","marks":["bold"],"text":"`RemoveObject`-style non-cascading discipline kept"},{"id":"spn-46068","text":": "},{"id":"spn-46069","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-46070","text":" never repairs a"}]}],"id":"blk-32681","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":6},{"id":"blk-32683","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46071","text":"scaffold. Subject drift is an error, not an auto-sync."}]},{"id":"blk-32684","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-46072","text":"7. Not built (deferred, per ruling)"}]},{"id":"blk-32685","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46073","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-46074","text":" (splits), "},{"id":"spn-46075","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors/--mcp"},{"id":"spn-46076","text":" (adapters over the Episode Kernel), "},{"id":"spn-46077","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-46078","text":", and the REPL. §7's order puts "},{"id":"spn-46079","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-46080","text":" next; "},{"id":"spn-46081","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-46082","text":" needs the D5 process model, which is specified but unbuilt."}]},{"id":"blk-32686","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-46083","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraxp23syv6xoqytdiiqdcttayrwzogtv4c7ul2cclt6oeztxmoe73a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}